  "A targeted \"propaganda\" strike (not a missile). Aim at a foreign country — the game draws a \"flag\" (a 3:2 rectangle with the letter T in the center). Flag size depends on the SHARE of troops invested: from ~13 tiles tall at a small share up to ~80 at full. The target's tiles inside the flag split up: the BASE of the flag (everything but the T) goes to a new separatist bot \"Independent {nick}\" — permanently immune to collapse, in a short alliance with you for {0}s and with the victim for {1}s. And the letter T — the loyal core — STAYS WITH THE VICTIM on a {2}s timer: the victim must carve a corridor from the T to their main land in time — succeed and they keep it, fail and the surrounded T is absorbed by the separatist. Cast cost: {3} gold plus the invested troops (they burn and set the flag size; the separatist's population is multiplied by {4} so the new country is viable). If fewer than {5} target tiles fall in the flag base, the split doesn't fire and nothing is spent.",
