  "Revanchism slows conquest of your land across your whole territory — up to {0}× slower, the more you've been cut back from your historic peak. It does not raise the attacker's troop cost.",
  "Rows with fewer than {0} picks show no Δ. Ultimates missing from the table were not picked in this period — or are not in the game right now.",
  "Shoots down enemy missiles, drones and airborne assaults. Range grows with level: {0} tiles at level 1, about {1} at level 5, capped at {2}. Reload {3}s. A SAM fires with LEAD: it computes where the missile will enter its radius and shoots there, so the radius is strictly enforced. Its interceptor flies at speed {4} — faster than a nuke ({5}), which is why it catches up. Against MIRV it works differently: a ready SAM shields its whole radius from the warheads, spending its charge to do it. It takes longer to build than any other regular building — {6}s — so tearing one down is easier than waiting it out.",
  "Skin “{0}” created. Play under this nick to see it.",
  "Spawns trade ships to other players' ports — they carry gold, and the amount scales with DISTANCE, not level. A port's level = how many ship-spawn rolls it makes and how many times it appears in others' trade-target lists, so a level-5 port is roughly five separate ports by throughput. Separate ports, though, cover different waters and give different distances — and distance is money. A port also repairs your warships: a level-N port heals up to N ships at once, +{0} healing rate per level. With nobody to trade with (an island, all foreign ports dead) a port starts shipping to itself — you need at least two of your own ports, {1}s cooldown.",
  "Stadium: while it stands, population growth and gold income are +{0}%. CAST \"Olympic Games\" ({1}): world peace for {2}s — everyone is everyone's friend: no attacks, ships don't fire, SAMs don't intercept (missiles still fly), attacks under way are recalled. The stadium bonus rises to +{3}% for the duration. {4} min cooldown. Unlocked by the \"Olympic reserve\" achievement (earn {5} gold over your career) or for 500 blood diamonds.",
  "Stands for {0}s, then lapses. You can ask the same player again no sooner than {1}s later.",
